WEBVTT

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:10.590
Wiping off my tears.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.300
I'm starting to run now

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:18.560
Tomorrow I'll be born anew.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:24.370
How could "you always be my friend"?

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:29.280
That person's word makes me more courageous.

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:33.480
There are times when it's possible I will be depressed

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:38.580
and there are times when things are delightful.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:45.170
I'll always be

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:51.020
next to you.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.910
Smiling 100%

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.450
Striking 100%

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:03.640
I've come so far.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.560
Being 100% pure

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.190
The things I want to tell you

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:14.670
change to treasure completely.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.190
in the 100% case

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:20.950
Even if it's a long distance,

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:27.280
I'll still say I would meet you with the same feelings.

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.580
What do you do, mister?

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:42.710
I’m a... detective.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:43.920
Detective?

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.930
That's somebody who catches bad guys, right?

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:49.550
Catching them is the police’s work.

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:52.260
My job comes ahead of that;

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:57.310
I solve mysteries that are all tangled up.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:00.020
Wow... amazing!

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:01.650
Here you go!

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:04.030
Thanks, Mr. Detective!

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:08.990
You're wearing a ring even though you're a guy?

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:11.030
Strange?

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:14.370
But I really like it.

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:18.670
See? It’s got a profile of Sherlock Holmes on it.

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:20.040
Well?

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:21.000
Cool huh?

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:30.220
It sure is, mister!

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:33.220
Kyuu!

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:34.720
Kyuu.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:37.600
Huh?

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:40.400
I fell out again...

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:42.860
I'm sorry, Ryuu.

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:47.650
You always fall out, but today you were also mumbling in your sleep.

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:52.280
I was having a nice dream.

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:53.370
Dream?

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:57.450
A dream about my favorite old man.

00:03:58.730 --> 00:03:59.410
Old man?

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:03.460
Dan Morihiko, Kidnapped!

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:31.450
It’s been 8 years, hasn’t it?

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:33.240
Yeah...

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:36.990
If he hadn’t shielded me then at the cost of his life,

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:38.830
I'd be...

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:44.670
The days go by fast.

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:18.740
Are you OK, Katagiri-kun?

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:21.080
Yeah.

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:24.500
Who are you?

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:25.630
Dan-sensei?

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:28.170
I don’t need you!

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:29.880
Katagiri-kun!

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:40.470
Hey Ryuu.

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:45.100
I’m going to the library until its time to go to DDS.

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:46.060
What?

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:48.650
How did you know what I was going to ask?

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:49.940
Just got a feeling.

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:52.570
I wonder if its because we're together everyday.

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:55.280
Really, it’s like telepathy!

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:59.910
They say that people who truly trust each other

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:02.250
can hear each other’s voices in their heart even if they're far apart.

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:03.790
In their heart?

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:04.620
Yup!

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:08.330
I hope both of you become such good friends.

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:12.510
I wonder if we can.

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:19.100
Yes yes.

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:21.060
oh
It’s from DDS!

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:21.810
It’s from Ops!

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:24.770
Yes, this is Kyuu!

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:30.190
Dan-sensei has?

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:32.440
Yes, I'll be right there!

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:38.280
Any contact from the criminal?

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:40.450
No, not yet.

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:43.200
Damn, why did this happen?

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:47.120
I’m sorry... I couldn’t protect him...

00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:49.380
No, it’s not your fault Katagiri-sensei.

00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:52.300
Calm down Touyama!

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:55.670
I can’t calm down; Dan-sensei’s been kidnapped!

00:06:55.700 --> 00:07:00.090
No matter who the victim is, a detective needs
to be calm and rationally think things through.

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:02.640
Dan-sensei taught you that, didn’t he?

00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:13.270
Yes, this is DDS.

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:14.820
/

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:15.860
Hello?

00:07:16.130 --> 00:07:18.740
We have your principal.

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:20.740
Here are our demands:

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:24.040
Get one billion yen ready in one hour.

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:25.500
What?

00:07:25.850 --> 00:07:27.330
That’s impossible to do in one hour!

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:29.210
Give us more time

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:30.830
That won’t work...

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:33.750
Look at the screen in your room.

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:39.300
Dan sensei!
Dan-sensei!

00:07:40.450 --> 00:07:41.800
Is he just fainted?

00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:42.640
His voice!

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:43.760
Let us hear his voice!

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:45.350
Don’t worry.

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:47.930
He’s just asleep.

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:50.690
If you can’t get the money ready,

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:53.110
then the time bomb will go off,

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:59.200
and your beloved principle will be blown to bits.

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:04.990
Listen, you've got one hour and no more.

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:06.450
I'll contact you later.

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:08.870
Kazuma, can you trace it?

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:10.830
No, they've got control over the line

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:12.460
I can't

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:15.130
They did manage to kidnap Dan-sensei;

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:20.340
they do clean work with no holes.

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:24.760
Could they be connected to Pluto?

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:27.350
I think it’s safe to assume that.

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:32.560
This is...

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:34.060
What is it?

00:08:34.420 --> 00:08:36.480
It’s a rescue signal from Dan-sensei!

00:08:37.090 --> 00:08:38.190
I'll put it on the screen.

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:42.660
The warehouse district in Port Kusetomi!

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:44.870
Hongou sensei!

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:47.910
He’s not calm at all, is he?

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:57.800
But boss, don’t you think one billion is a little much?

00:08:58.110 --> 00:09:00.010
I’m not the one who decided it.

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:02.050
If you have any problems with it, tell them.

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:06.430
Well, for us the more the better, though.

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:10.180
It’s me.

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:15.020
What?

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:17.190
Hey, old man!

00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:19.280
Enough playing around!

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:24.820
You’re screwing with us aren’t you...

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:30.540
A transmitter.

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:32.330
We're done for.

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:37.840
Seems like whoever is behind you has good ears.

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:39.840
Then you understand.

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:45.800
The signal’s gone!

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:46.800
What?

00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:48.010
Why?

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:49.470
It's no good, I can’t get it again

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:51.560
No way, that can’t mean...

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:53.180
Nanami-sensei, hurry!

00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:54.390
Don’t worry.

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:55.440
We're almost there.

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:07.990
Warehouse East-7.

00:10:08.390 --> 00:10:10.160
This is where the signal came from.

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:12.160
Alight, I'll go on ahead.

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:13.870
You all stay here.

00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:14.540
OK!

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:42.190
Hongou!

00:10:42.260 --> 00:10:43.280
Nanami!

00:10:43.670 --> 00:10:44.690
You?

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:50.830
When I got here the place was already empty.

00:10:51.470 --> 00:10:52.490
Dammit...

00:10:56.900 --> 00:10:59.790
This is... Dan-sensei’s cuff-link!

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:02.210
He was here then!

00:11:02.570 --> 00:11:04.630
But why?

00:11:04.820 --> 00:11:07.380
Damn... we were so close.

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:09.300
Kyuu!

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:10.890
What?

00:11:11.740 --> 00:11:12.430
Look at that!

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:20.060
This is bad!

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:21.160
Run!

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:44.750
Is everybody OK?

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:46.460
Somehow!

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:51.260
Sorry Megu!

00:11:51.830 --> 00:11:53.890
No, thank you.

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:13.320
Yes?

00:12:13.350 --> 00:12:14.530
This is DDS.

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:17.950
Lets stop the games.

00:12:18.310 --> 00:12:23.040
We've put this in an abandoned lot next to
the Seiou shopping center for insurance.

00:12:24.070 --> 00:12:25.130
Do they mean this?

00:12:25.150 --> 00:12:26.500
That’s a dumpster!

00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:31.470
Throw the one billion yen in there by ten o'clock.

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:34.550
Any funny business and this time...

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:37.720
You know what'll happen.

00:12:39.370 --> 00:12:40.520
Katagiri-sensei!

00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:47.780
We'll give them what they want.

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:51.860
Seiou shopping center?

00:12:51.970 --> 00:12:52.570
Yes.

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:55.160
As soon as we're ready we'll head there.

00:12:55.310 --> 00:12:55.950
Roger.

00:12:56.680 --> 00:12:57.410
Hey guys.

00:12:57.850 --> 00:12:58.450
What?

00:12:58.480 --> 00:12:59.410
It’s really cramped here.

00:12:59.730 --> 00:13:00.410
Quiet.

00:13:01.100 --> 00:13:03.290
There may be a spy here.

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:05.040
A spy?

00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:08.380
And one very close.

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:09.710
What do you mean?

00:13:09.990 --> 00:13:11.760
The enemy's moving way too fast

00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:15.680
It’s impossible that we could be that transparent.

00:13:16.030 --> 00:13:16.390
I get it, "4

00:13:16.410 --> 00:13:16.720
get it, “4

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:21.600
You wouldn’t normally notice that a transmitter was concealed in a cuff-link.

00:13:21.620 --> 00:13:27.650
So there’s a possibility that there’s a spy among the people
who were in the room when we got that signal.

00:13:27.710 --> 00:13:32.490
At that point there was the A and Q-Class, Katagiri-sensei,

00:13:32.510 --> 00:13:35.620
Nanami-sensei, and Hongou-sensei in the room.

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:40.040
Hongou-sensei ran out of the room and was
the first person to get into the warehouse.

00:13:40.350 --> 00:13:42.830
I think he’s suspicious too.

00:13:42.850 --> 00:13:46.460
He was a bit weird in Jinchuumura too.

00:13:46.730 --> 00:13:50.300
It’s true that there are a lot of things Hongou-sensei
does that we can’t understand.

00:13:50.690 --> 00:13:51.380
Nanami sensei!

00:13:51.400 --> 00:13:52.720
You heard us?

00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:59.760
I have eyes like a hawk and ears like a bat.

00:13:59.790 --> 00:14:01.020
You didn’t know, did you?

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:01.890
Nope.

00:14:03.670 --> 00:14:06.440
But it’s dangerous to just decide that it’s Hongou.

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:11.070
Everybody who was there then is equally a suspect.

00:14:12.050 --> 00:14:14.400
Including you, yes?

00:14:15.550 --> 00:14:16.910
Yup.

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:28.540
Then, Hongou-sensei. . .

00:14:36.740 --> 00:14:37.720
Where’s the stuff?

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:43.020
We checked in the box too but there was nothing suspicious.

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:46.230
It’s almost ten.

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:49.230
Let’s all hide and watch the box.

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:50.440
Ok.

00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:58.410
But how are they gonna get the money out of there?

00:14:59.350 --> 00:15:02.910
That’s right... at an easily viewable place like this...

00:15:16.860 --> 00:15:19.430
Dammit, I can’t see past that truck.

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:20.680
Really!

00:15:31.620 --> 00:15:32.410
The box!

00:15:33.510 --> 00:15:34.320
Let’s follow it!

00:15:34.340 --> 00:15:34.980
OK.

00:15:37.430 --> 00:15:38.740
We need to go too.

00:15:38.760 --> 00:15:39.740
No, wait.

00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:42.740
Leave that to Hongou and the A-Class.

00:15:45.890 --> 00:15:46.660
Yeah...

00:15:47.890 --> 00:15:49.460
Got it.

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:53.750
Went well, just like we planned.

00:15:54.440 --> 00:15:56.550
Our pans are our perfect.

00:15:57.110 --> 00:15:58.550
Of course it did.

00:16:03.990 --> 00:16:06.430
There should still be some kind of clue.

00:16:15.170 --> 00:16:15.860
This is...

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:22.670
What's wrong Kyuu?

00:16:25.970 --> 00:16:27.040
That’s strange.

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:30.870
Everybody hide!

00:16:31.230 --> 00:16:32.210
What's wrong?

00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:35.800
That truck could be a dummy.

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:04.200
What's wrong, Miss Yurie?

00:17:05.220 --> 00:17:06.780
What are you afraid of?

00:17:08.140 --> 00:17:09.790
Is this really OK?

00:17:10.940 --> 00:17:13.920
If King Hades finds this out...

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:20.840
We must atone for our failure with Ryuu-sama.

00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:23.880
Well...

00:17:24.160 --> 00:17:29.850
And a great failure can only be atoned for with great success.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.850
Don’t worry.

00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:39.610
King Hades will be pleased for a long time.

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:54.790
Weed d it!

00:17:54.810 --> 00:17:59.170
Even DDS is no match for us!

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:03.170
But bro, is it Okay to let the hostage go?

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:05.050
We've got the money!

00:18:05.070 --> 00:18:07.340
Who cares about the geezer?

00:18:07.780 --> 00:18:10.510
Pluto can do what they want with him.

00:18:12.460 --> 00:18:13.520
No sense in staying;

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:14.440
let’s get out of here!

00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:15.230
Alright.

00:18:19.420 --> 00:18:22.650
You are surrounded!

00:18:22.970 --> 00:18:28.200
Come along quietly with your hands up!

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:29.490
What?

00:18:29.510 --> 00:18:31.040
Impossible!

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:33.000
You're late.

00:18:33.350 --> 00:18:35.160
We were getting sick of waiting.

00:18:35.190 --> 00:18:36.250
Why?

00:18:36.270 --> 00:18:38.210
How did you find us?

00:18:38.230 --> 00:18:39.540
There were two hints.

00:18:39.730 --> 00:18:41.840
The first was the bind spot on the hill.

00:18:42.900 --> 00:18:45.720
The second was the fact that the entire box was gone.

00:18:46.280 --> 00:18:47.430
And there’s one answer.

00:18:48.370 --> 00:18:54.810
You hid under a vinyl sheet at that construction site long before we got there.

00:18:55.330 --> 00:18:58.900
And then the semi stopped at the nearby traffic light,

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:03.400
and at that moment our view was blocked

00:19:03.420 --> 00:19:05.650
and moved it to our blind spot on the beach.

00:19:06.300 --> 00:19:10.450
Then, while it was blocking our vision you carried
the box down and covered it with the sheet.

00:19:11.310 --> 00:19:17.830
If that huge box disappeared in front of your eyes,
you'd probably think the truck carried it off right?

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:27.170
You were going to wait until we followed the truck,
and then cart it off when there was nobody left.

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:35.810
But we noticed that trick, and you didn’t notice us hiding.

00:19:36.460 --> 00:19:39.900
We saw you carry off the money

00:19:41.460 --> 00:19:43.570
in that boat.

00:19:46.220 --> 00:19:49.610
And we saw you go from boat to the car too.

00:19:49.640 --> 00:19:53.200
I've got perfect vision, you know!

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:54.950
Old man, the rest is yours!

00:19:54.980 --> 00:19:56.750
OK, arrest them!

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:04.000
Ouch!

00:20:04.190 --> 00:20:06.960
Heh, you've grown up Kintarou!

00:20:07.070 --> 00:20:09.430
Don’t say it like that!

00:20:11.700 --> 00:20:13.800
Katagiri-sensei, let’s find Dan-sensei!

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:16.060
Ye-yeah...

00:20:16.290 --> 00:20:17.980
What's wrong Sensei?

00:20:18.040 --> 00:20:19.270
N-nothing.

00:20:19.540 --> 00:20:25.610
It’s just that the first time I saw you at DDS you
didn’t seem impressive and I was worried,

00:20:25.630 --> 00:20:27.570
but you've really gotten good.

00:20:30.510 --> 00:20:34.160
You're under arrest for kidnapping and extortion!

00:20:48.780 --> 00:20:50.420
Calm down!

00:20:50.990 --> 00:20:51.800
What's wrong?

00:20:53.200 --> 00:20:54.220
Old man!

00:21:06.550 --> 00:21:07.980
What is this?

00:21:09.630 --> 00:21:10.690
Hypnosis.

00:21:11.340 --> 00:21:15.700
They were programmed to do this the moment they were handcuffed.

00:21:15.850 --> 00:21:18.240
That means it is Pluto!

00:21:18.270 --> 00:21:21.040
They weren’t after the money in the first place!

00:21:21.060 --> 00:21:21.870
Then...

00:21:21.900 --> 00:21:22.960
Dan-sensei Is...

00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:23.870
Find him!

00:21:24.150 --> 00:21:25.380
We need to look too!

00:21:29.990 --> 00:21:31.170
Where are you?

00:21:31.570 --> 00:21:32.970
Sensei!

00:21:32.700 --> 00:21:32.970
Dan sensei!

00:21:32.700 --> 00:21:34.340
Dan sensei!

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:37.890
Dan-sensei. . .

00:21:38.870 --> 00:21:40.390
Amakusa, Kyuu!

00:21:42.120 --> 00:21:42.940
What is it,

00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:43.980
Hongou-sense?

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:46.770
It’s you.

00:21:47.130 --> 00:21:49.270
You may have noticed already,

00:21:51.800 --> 00:21:53.780
but there’s a spy among us.

00:21:57.220 --> 00:21:58.990
You don’t seem surprised.

00:22:01.230 --> 00:22:02.710
Did you think it was me?

00:22:03.730 --> 00:22:06.080
Do you know who the spy is?

00:22:06.860 --> 00:22:11.460
No, but it seems you may have.

00:22:12.950 --> 00:22:14.050
Well, whatever.

00:22:14.280 --> 00:22:16.340
Anyway, just don’t let your guard down for anybody.

00:22:21.330 --> 00:22:21.810
Dan sensei!

00:22:21.960 --> 00:22:22.390
Dan sensei!

00:22:22.410 --> 00:22:26.400
Dan-sensei, Saburoumaru is here to save you!

00:22:26.420 --> 00:22:27.980
Dan sensei!

00:22:27.790 --> 00:22:30.690
It’s me the Tokyo University student Saburomaru Yutaka!

00:22:31.800 --> 00:22:33.190
Could he have been sitting here?

00:22:36.390 --> 00:22:37.110
This is...

00:22:39.810 --> 00:22:40.490
Kyuu!

00:22:40.890 --> 00:22:43.450
This is a message Dan-sensei left for us!

00:22:44.230 --> 00:22:44.830
What?

00:22:44.850 --> 00:22:45.500
Did fou find something?

00:22:45.520 --> 00:22:47.210
Everybody, over here!

00:23:00.950 --> 00:23:01.970
T-This is...

00:23:02.040 --> 00:23:03.520
The old detective...

00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:09.150
This is an emergency message.

00:23:09.880 --> 00:23:15.740
I have something I'd like to report about Sir Anubis.

00:23:24.180 --> 00:23:25.160
Sir Anubis...

00:23:27.270 --> 00:23:32.040
This is for the best, isn’t it?

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:51.770
Somehow it's collapsing

00:23:51.800 --> 00:23:54.140
Embracing such a feeling.

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:55.030
Flowing.

00:23:55.050 --> 00:23:58.910
I'd be worried tomorrow.

00:23:58.930 --> 00:24:01.120
If the same thing happened.

00:24:01.140 --> 00:24:02.120
Go wrong.

00:24:02.130 --> 00:24:06.460
He looks up at the sky, pondering

00:24:06.470 --> 00:24:09.020
You're very far away.

00:24:09.930 --> 00:24:13.180
Show your heart if you have the courage

00:24:13.190 --> 00:24:16.310
passing the border line.

00:24:16.330 --> 00:24:19.760
In order to get past, I walk against the wind

00:24:19.770 --> 00:24:23.400
and I can finish a battle.

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:26.940
When I feel like an abandoned child

00:24:26.970 --> 00:24:30.360
then I'll stand in line with you.

00:24:30.390 --> 00:24:33.930
Facing the wind, I forget,

00:24:33.940 --> 00:24:37.540
somehow this is the only important thing.

00:24:37.550 --> 00:24:40.290
We protect, because there Is no return.

00:24:40.310 --> 00:24:41.890
It's becoming dearly.

00:24:41.920 --> 00:24:45.840
Today I embrace, right now I conquer.

00:24:47.010 --> 00:24:55.960
Next Episode

00:24:47.430 --> 00:24:52.460
Kidnapped Dan-sensei: the final battle which will be solved on the ocean.

00:24:52.770 --> 00:24:56.710
Overcoming the many difficulties, everyone’s heart becomes one.

00:24:57.240 --> 00:25:00.760
Q Class VS Anubis, who will be the winner?

00:25:00.780 --> 00:25:02.380
of the direct clash?

00:25:02.870 --> 00:25:04.180
There can be only one!

00:25:07.160 --> 00:25:12.310
I'm sorry that I can only give you a wedding in secret like this.

00:25:12.670 --> 00:25:14.770
I know.
